sections.s5b_flow:
```
  ═══ WITHOUT volatile: JIT HOISTING ═══

  Worker thread (JIT compiled):
  register = running;           ← read ONCE (hoisted!)
  while (register) {            ← uses cached value FOREVER
      doWork();
  }
  // register = true FOREVER! Never reads main memory again!

  Main thread:
  running = false;              ← written to main memory
  // Worker's register is NOT updated! INVISIBLE!

  ═══ WITH volatile: NO HOISTING ═══

  Worker thread:
  while (running) {             ← volatile read EVERY iteration
      // reads main memory → sees latest value
      doWork();
  }
  // running = false → sees it → loop exits!

  ═══ JIT OPTIMIZATION (legal under JMM) ═══
  Before JIT:  while (running) { ... }     // reads memory each time
  After JIT:   boolean r = running;         // read ONCE
               while (r) { ... }            // cached! Infinite!
  volatile:    prevents this optimization!
```
